  "body": "Three-method AMD MI350X numerical evidence for independently selected SGLang packed RMSNorm at width16384, native block1024/physical wave64 and logical32 reductions.\n\nBoth mi350 and mi350-2 completed 24 cases x three methods = 144 launches total. All 190,513,152 freshly recomputed CPU float64 comparisons pass atol=rtol=0.002. All original-adaptation, guarded-repair and upstream-body output streams match bit for bit across both hosts in these finite trials. The independent CPU Torch FP32 reference has 1,734 recorded bit differences.\n\nThe four assets retain every frozen FP16 input and weight, all three complete output streams per host, binaries, every compiler-reported source/header, independent auditors, prelaunch activity history and thirteen fully rehashed rejection controls. Allocation canaries and read-only buffers remain intact. The original template body is retained verbatim with explicit HIP helper substitutions and -ffp-contract=off.\n\nThe native source proof currently reaches the first logical32 XOR snapshot after preparing all 64 physical lanes; 356 axiom audits, independent frozen replay, eleven false proof claims and twenty-two metadata controls pass. SGLang whole-kernel execution and dense-real equality remain pending; source certificates: zero. The original access-model shared-write race remains distinct from the equal finite numerical outputs.\n\nZero model calls. Original paper model pass rates, token costs and NVIDIA measurements remain unreproduced. CUDA helper/compiler and IEEE equivalence are not claimed.\n"
